{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c997d9fd-b72f-438b-aa2f-2522721a6a65","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The task **EXP-006: Concurrency-Safe Transactional Ledger with Real-Time Dashboard \u0026 E2E Validation** was planned, executed, and verified under the workspace ICM pipeline:\n\n### Summary of Artifacts \u0026 Contracts\n\n1. **ICM Contracts**:\n   - [`01_intake.md`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tasks/TSK-015/01_intake.md): Problem definition, double-entry and non-negative balance invariants, idempotency guarantees, and stage boundaries.\n   - [`02_plan.md`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tasks/TSK-015/02_plan.md): Technical architecture, asynchronous deadlock-free mutex lock coordinator, integer-cent monetary precision, and OKR acceptance criteria.\n   - [`03_exec.md`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tasks/TSK-015/03_exec.md): Implementation ledger across server, UI, and test suites.\n   - [`04_verify.md`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tasks/TSK-015/04_verify.md): Automated verification results with 100% pass rate.\n   - [`05_retro.md`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tasks/TSK-015/05_retro.md): System learnings, concurrency patterns, and architecture evaluation.\n\n2. **System Implementation**:\n   - **Backend Engine** ([`server.js`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/experiments/tasks/EXP-006/server.js)):\n     - Concurrency-safe double-entry ledger with integer-cent tracking preventing IEEE 754 floating-point drift.\n     - Deadlock-free asynchronous mutex lock coordinator (`acquire(sortedIds)` / `release()`).\n     - Idempotency key registry with cache-hit tracking preventing duplicate debits and replays.\n     - Live invariant audit checking system liquidity conservation ($\\sum \\text{balances} = \\$100,000.00$) and non-negativity ($\\forall a, \\text{balance}_a \\ge 0$).\n   - **Tailwind Dashboard** ([`public/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/experiments/tasks/EXP-006/public/index.html)):\n     - Dark-mode interface displaying live liquidity, invariant status pills, account cards, and audit transaction records.\n     - Optimistic UI updates, UUID generators, and explicit alert states for overdraft and duplicate key notifications.\n   - **Playwright E2E Suite** ([`tests/ledger.spec.js`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/experiments/tasks/EXP-006/tests/ledger.spec.js)):\n     - 5 headless automated tests: Initial ledger invariants, atomic transfers with UI updates, overdraft prevention, idempotency key deduplication, and high-concurrency race condition resistance under parallel load.\n\n### Verification Run\n\n```\n\u003e exp-006-concurrency-ledger@1.0.0 test\n\u003e playwright test\n\nRunning 5 tests using 1 worker\n  ok 1 tests\\ledger.spec.js: Initial Ledger State \u0026 Invariant Verification (335ms)\n  ok 2 tests\\ledger.spec.js: Atomic Double-Entry Transfer \u0026 UI Balance Update (427ms)\n  ok 3 tests\\ledger.spec.js: Balance Invariant \u0026 Overdraft Protection (Insufficient Funds) (350ms)\n  ok 4 tests\\ledger.spec.js: Idempotency Key Deduplication \u0026 Replay Protection (469ms)\n  ok 5 tests\\ledger.spec.js: High-Concurrency Race Condition Resistance \u0026 Zero-Sum Conservation (542ms)\n\n5 passed (3.4s)\n```\n","duration_seconds":27.0232921,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":88039,"output_tokens":1802,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":240829,"total_tokens":89841}}}
